IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pta-small-estates`
IMPORT `pta-qa`

-- Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (pta-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for every role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes the situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value
-- that makes it not hold and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the next of kin and the
-- will-maker (the baseline's seat) the answer is also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same
-- facts. For the beneficiary and the creditor the answers are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts: the baseline's fixtures, copied (Jake's death, k098, with the encoder's $600,000 apartment; Ruby assumed in WA
-- and willing, as the baseline assumed; the encoder's fee figures). Expected values are written by hand from the
-- deposited text, never copied from the output. The mechanical cases at the end are generated by the scratchpad script
-- gen_pta.py from the layer's own @export list.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked part` IS A `The Public Trustee's part`
ASSUME `an unasked estate` IS AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it`
ASSUME `an unasked family` IS A `What the family is doing`
ASSUME `an unasked Court` IS A `What the Court thinks`
ASSUME `an unasked dealing` IS A `My dealing with the Public Trustee`
ASSUME `an unasked charge` IS A `What the charge is for`
ASSUME `unasked fees` IS A `The fee facts`

`as next of kin` MEANS `I am next of kin of someone who has died`
`as will-maker` MEANS `I am making a will, or have made one`
`as beneficiary` MEANS `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers`
`as creditor` MEANS `I am owed money by someone who has died`

`an election` MEANS `it has filed a small-estate election (s 14)`
`administering` MEANS `it administers the estate under an order to administer, a grant, or as executor`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's, copied)`

-- An estate a fortnight after the death, as the layer asks it, with each value of `The will and who will act` (QA-5).
GIVEN `the will` IS A `The will and who will act`
GIVETH AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it`
`an estate a fortnight on, with` `the will` MEANS
    `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` WITH
        `the person who died left property in Western Australia` IS TRUE
        `they left property outside Western Australia` IS FALSE
        `the gross value in WA, as the Public Trustee estimates it` IS 638000
        `probate or administration has been taken out in WA` IS FALSE
        `days since they died` IS 14
        `full months since they died` IS 0
        `the will and who will act` IS `the will`


-- The baseline's fixtures, put as the layer asks them (QA-5): whether there is a will and who will act, from the
-- baseline's five facts, and the rest field for field. The cases that compare with the baseline pass the baseline the
-- fixtures themselves.
GIVEN e IS AN `The estate`
      f IS A `The family`
GIVETH A `The will and who will act`
`the will in` e f MEANS
    IF NOT e's `the deceased left a will`
    THEN IF f's `the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA`
         THEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA`
         ELSE `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA`
    ELSE IF f's `an executor named in the will is willing, capable and resident in WA`
         THEN IF f's `the will expressly prohibits the executor authorising the Public Trustee` THEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` ELSE `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA`
         ELSE IF f's `the executor renounced and everyone first entitled declined in writing filed in Court`
              THEN IF f's `the will expressly prohibits the executor authorising the Public Trustee` THEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` ELSE `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court`
              ELSE IF f's `the will expressly prohibits the executor authorising the Public Trustee` THEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` ELSE `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA`

GIVEN e IS AN `The estate`
      f IS A `The family`
GIVETH AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it`
`the layer's estate` e f MEANS
    `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` WITH
        `the person who died left property in Western Australia` IS e's `left property in Western Australia`
        `they left property outside Western Australia` IS e's `left property outside Western Australia`
        `the gross value in WA, as the Public Trustee estimates it` IS e's `gross value in Western Australia as estimated by the Public Trustee`
        `probate or administration has been taken out in WA` IS e's `someone has taken out probate or administration in Western Australia`
        `days since they died` IS e's `days since the death`
        `full months since they died` IS e's `full months since the death`
        `the will and who will act` IS `the will in` e f

GIVEN f IS A `The family`
GIVETH A `What the family is doing`
`the layer's family` f MEANS
    `What the family is doing` WITH
        `the estate is unprotected or liable to waste, and the family absent or not found` IS f's `the estate is unprotected or liable to waste and the family is absent or not found`
        `the estate is perishable, or in danger of being lost or destroyed` IS f's `the estate is perishable or in danger of being lost or destroyed`
        `how many persons are entitled to obtain administration` IS f's `persons entitled to obtain administration`
        `how many of them have authorised the Public Trustee to apply` IS f's `of them, persons who have authorised the Public Trustee to apply`


