§§ `For the next of kin of someone who has died`

-- s 12: the one person entitled, or a majority of several; not where the will prohibits the executor authorising.
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `three children, two authorising`) (`the layer's family` `three children, two authorising`) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `four children, two authorising`) (`the layer's family` `four children, two authorising`) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `a testate estate, a fortnight after the death` `the sole executor authorises, but the will prohibits it`) (`the layer's family` `the sole executor authorises, but the will prohibits it`) EQUALS no

-- s 10(1), s 12, Jake's death (k098): a fortnight on, Ruby in WA and not authorising, no ground; with her authority, s 12;
-- four months with no application, s 10(1)(c); Ruby overseas, s 10(1)(ab); a will with no executor in WA, s 10(1)(a).
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `no ground: the Public Trustee may not apply`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 12, the persons entitled have authorised the Public Trustee`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, four months on with no application` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(c), no application within 3 months of the death`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `Ruby, living overseas`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, living overseas`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(ab), the person first entitled is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `a testate estate, a fortnight after the death` `no executor willing and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `no executor willing and resident in WA`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(a), no willing, capable executor resident in WA`
#ASSERT `May the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, a fortnight after the death` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`the layer's estate` `Jake's estate, six weeks after the death` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, seeing no reasonable possibility of an application` EQUALS yes


-- QA-5, each value of `The will and who will act`, a fortnight after the death, with no one authorising and the Court
-- with no view: s 10(1)(ab) with no will and no one first entitled in WA; none with a willing executor in WA; s 10(1)(a)
-- with none (an executor who renounced is not "willing ... to act", and (a) comes first). s 12 with the one person
-- entitled authorising: yes, unless there is a will that "expressly prohibit[s]" the executor authorising (s 12(2)).
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `no ground: the Public Trustee may not apply`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(ab), the person first entitled is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `no ground: the Public Trustee may not apply`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `no ground: the Public Trustee may not apply`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(a), no willing, capable executor resident in WA`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(a), no willing, capable executor resident in WA`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(a), no willing, capable executor resident in WA`
#ASSERT `On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, in WA and willing, not authorising the Public Trustee`) `the Court, with no view` EQUALS `the answer is` `s 10(1)(a), no willing, capable executor resident in WA`
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` `as next of kin` (`an estate a fortnight on, with` `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`) (`the layer's family` `Ruby, having authorised the Public Trustee`) EQUALS no

-- s 10(1)(ab) proviso: Ruby, in WA, entitled, applying: yes.
